 ## Overview
-Variance Regularization reduces ambiguity in low-texture and few-shot regions of indoor scenes by constraining the variance of the weight distribution $w(\mathbf{r})$ and color distribution $c(\mathbf{r}, d)$ along rays [S1]. Unlike standard photometric losses which may allow identical rendered colors from vastly different weight distributions, this method penalizes deviations in depth expectation and color consistency relative to the rendered pixel values [S1]. It serves as a supplement to photometric loss, particularly effective where geometric cues are sparse [S1].
+Variance Regularization reduces ambiguity in low-texture and few-shot regions of indoor scenes by constraining the variance of the weight distribution $w(\mathbf{r})$ and color distribution $c(\mathbf{r}, d)$ along rays [S1]. Unlike standard photometric losses, which may permit identical rendered colors from vastly different weight distributions, this method penalizes deviations in depth expectation and color consistency relative to the rendered pixel values [S1]. It serves as a supplement to photometric loss, particularly effective where geometric cues are sparse [S1].
 
